          "message": "telo-workspace.yaml: 'release.units.1' (b) declares no 'version:' and none of its ecosystems (npm) keeps a version. Declare 'version:', naming the file that holds it.",
          "path": [
            "release",
            "units",
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "code": "WORKSPACE_INVALID_VALUE",
          "severity": "error",
          "message": "telo-workspace.yaml: anchor 'x' of 'npm' is listed twice.",
          "path": [
            "release",
            "units",
            5,
            "ecosystem",
            "npm",
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "code": "WORKSPACE_ANCHOR_INVALID",
          "severity": "error",
          "message": "telo-workspace.yaml: anchor 3 of 'npm' is not a literal directory inside the unit. An anchor is a unit-relative path with no pattern and no '..' (or '.' for the unit itself).",
          "path": [
            "release",
            "units",
            5,
            "ecosystem",
            "npm",
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "code": "WORKSPACE_INVALID_VALUE",
          "severity": "error",
          "message": "telo-workspace.yaml: 'payload' is reserved for a declared payload and names no ecosystem. Declare a payload with the entry's 'payload:' key.",
